WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.020
In this video, you will tour the dashboard a lighting company sees after signing in: your numbers, your homes, your details, and your activity.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:09.720
We start on the map.

00:00:10.902 --> 00:00:12.662
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.420
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.260
Then tap Allow.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.580
Once your profile is yours, sign in and open your dashboard.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.900
It has four tabs.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:38.360
Overview shows your numbers: profile views over the last thirty days, the homes on the map that name your company, and the quote requests you have received.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:39.940
Tap Homes.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.860
Homes that name your company wait here for your answer.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.160
Confirm the ones you really installed, so visitors see the check mark.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:50.880
Tap Details.

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:59.740
This is where you set how people reach you: your phone, your website, the areas you serve, and a short About blurb.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.900
It all shows on your public page.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.200
Below that is your logo.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:09.420
A logo makes your company easy to spot, on your page and in the homes you installed.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.120
Tap Activity.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:20.400
See how many people looked at your profile each day, and read the quote requests families sent you, with their email and phone.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.120
That is your installer dashboard.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.700
Check it often, so no quote request waits.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.640
Next up: Sponsor your installer company.

